mk("giovanni","Don Giovanni",["Don Giovanni"],W,[
("premiere",None,"Don Giovanni premiered in Prague at the National Theatre (today\u2019s Estates Theatre) on 29 October 1787.","now called the Estates Theatre, on 29 October 1787"),
("blooper",None,"It was meant to open on 14 October 1787 for a visiting archduchess, but wasn\u2019t ready, so Le Nozze di Figaro was played instead.","it was not ready in time and Le nozze di Figaro was substituted","Composition_and_premiere"),
("history",None,"Prague commissioned it after Mozart\u2019s successful visit there in early 1787.","The opera was commissioned after the success of Mozart's trip to Prague in January and February 1787.","Composition_and_premiere"),
("music","Overture|Sinfonia","The overture opens with a thundering D minor cadence and a mysterious passage, then turns into a light-hearted D major allegro.","The overture begins with a thundering D minor cadence, followed by a short misterioso sequence which leads into a light-hearted D major allegro.","Act_1"),
("music","Madamina|catalogo","The Catalogue Aria counts the Don\u2019s conquests: 640 in Italy, 231 in Germany, 100 in France, 91 in Turkey, and in Spain, 1,003.","his conquests include 640 women and girls in Italy, 231 in Germany, 100 in France, 91 in Turkey, but in Spain, 1,003","Act_1"),
("history","Madamina|catalogo","Thanks to this aria, German and other languages call fold-out brochures a \u201cLeporello list\u201d.","provided the name \"Leporello list\" for pamphlets","Cultural_influence"),
("music","L\u00e0 ci darem|La ci darem","\u201cL\u00e0 ci darem la mano\u201d (\u201cThere we will entwine our hands\u201d): alone with Zerlina, the Don immediately turns on the charm.","Don Giovanni and Zerlina are soon alone and he immediately begins his seductive arts","Act_1"),
("music","Fin ch.han dal vino","The \u201cChampagne Aria\u201d: the Don orders a party with every girl Leporello can find.","tells Leporello to organise a party and invite every girl he can find","Act_1"),
("composer","Dalla sua pace","Mozart added \u201cDalla sua pace\u201d for the 1788 Vienna production, written for the tenor Francesco Morella.","Don Ottavio's aria \"Dalla sua pace\" (K. 540a, composed on 24 April for the tenor Francesco Morella)","Revision_for_Vienna"),
("composer","Mi trad\u00ec|In quali eccessi","Elvira\u2019s \u201cMi trad\u00ec quell\u2019alma ingrata\u201d was also a Vienna addition, composed on 30 April 1788 for Caterina Cavalieri.","composed on 30 April for the soprano Caterina Cavalieri","Revision_for_Vienna"),
("staging","Don Giovanni, a cenar|cenar teco|Commendatore","In Prague and Vienna one singer played both Masetto and the Commendatore. The demons\u2019 chorus gave him just a little time to change costume.",["the same singer played both Masetto and the Commendatore roles in both the Prague and Vienna premieres","gives the singer time for a costume change before entering as Masetto for the sextet, though not much time"],"Later_performance_traditions"),
("history","Questo \u00e8 il fin|Questo e il fin|Ah, dov.\u00e8 il perfido","A memoirist claimed the final ensemble was heard only at the first Prague performance, then never again during the original run. Today it is almost always performed.",["the final ensemble was only presented at the first performance in Prague, then never heard again during the original run","the final ensemble is almost invariably performed in full today"],"Later_performance_traditions"),
("critic",None,"Kierkegaard argued that \u201camong all classic works Don Giovanni stands highest.\u201d Gounod called it \u201ca work without blemish, of uninterrupted perfection\u201d.",["among all classic works Don Giovanni stands highest.","a work without blemish, of uninterrupted perfection"],"Cultural_influence"),
])
